<title>GERMANY: Holzmann says mgt duties not violated.</title>
<headline>Holzmann says mgt duties not violated.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Philip Holzmann AG said on Friday that an external audit of its management board showed it did not violate its duties in regard to losses on real estate.</p>
<p>Holzmann said the audit was conducted by the accounting firm KPMG.</p>
<p>Holzmann ran into financial problems in 1995, posting an expected loss of 443 million marks which forced it to omit its dividend payout. At the root of the problem were 458 million marks of write-downs on its property portfolio.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
